<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Real Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1994</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Plano Real</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Real Plan, or Plano Real, was the economic stabilisation programme that ended chronic hyperinflation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1994. Prepared under finance minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-henrique-cardoso">Fernando Henrique Cardoso</a>, it introduced a transitional unit of account, the URV, and then a new currency, the real, launched on 1 July 1994. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">Inflation</a>, which had exceeded 2,000 per cent in 1993, fell to single figures within a few years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/real-plan.jpg" alt="Real Plan" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph: User:Avelludo. Design: Central Bank of Brazil. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1-real-2019-25-anos.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
